  let s4 = `<div class="report-section" id="rs4"><h2>04 / Results — what works, what needs improvement</h2><p><b>Results snapshot:</b> ${rankings.map(x => `${x.p}: ${x.st.n} available visibility observations${x.top ? ` (leader: ${esc(x.top.title)})` : ''}`).join('; ')}.</p><p><b>Potentially working:</b> The strongest post per objective/metric should be investigated, rather than choosing one all-purpose winning post. Review hooks, media, narrative specificity and audience origin alongside comparable snapshots.</p><p><b>Needs improvement:</b> Missing/unsupported fields, sparse samples and posts with asset gaps reduce confidence. Compare underperformers against the median for their own format and channel.</p><p><b>Next test:</b> Select one creative variable to change (e.g. hook), keep format and audience objective similar, and evaluate at 48 hours, 7 days and 30 days.</p><p><b>Outliers:</b> Use Tukey upper fences Q3 + 1.5(Q3 − Q1) with eligibility checks; never quietly remove strong outliers from reporting.</p></div>`;
